   941	# PLAN-183 W5 (OQ-5 — ratified route (ii) WITH AMENDMENT, Owner 2026-08-24)
   942	# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   943	# WHO receives the docs/ + .github/ delivery this run. install.sh gates BOTH
   944	# of its delivery functions on `CEREMONY != user` (install.sh:1484, :1525), so
   945	# the upgrade route has to agree or the two diverge by construction.
   946	#
   947	# But the fail-SAFE resolution above answers "user" for EVERY pre-Wave-B
   948	# install (no install-state file at all) — which is exactly the HISTORICAL
   949	# ADOPTER population this delivery exists to reach. The debate measured it:
   950	# route (ii) without an amendment delivers to nobody who needs it, and the
   951	# pinned e2e is structurally blind to that because install.sh @ v1.2.0 already
   952	# writes install-state (class C2, "a Check that only exercises the pinned path
   953	# passes vacuously"). Hence --blind-install-state on the parity e2e.
   954	#
   955	# The ratified amendment: install-state unreadable/absent BUT
   956	# `.claude/.framework-version` present => the directory IS an existing
   957	# framework install => DELIVER. The marker is the evidence the fail-safe
   958	# throws away. A directory with NEITHER keeps today's default and gets
   959	# nothing.
   960	#
   961	# TWO PROPERTIES THIS DELIBERATELY KEEPS — both are the amendment, not
   962	# timidity about it:
   963	#   1. `_CEREMONY_PERSIST` stays "0". The inference must never reach the state
   964	#      file (:801-803: only RECORDED or EXPLICIT resolutions persist).
   965	#      Persisting an inference would make ONE missed migration permanent and
   966	#      would outrank a later real `--ceremony` flag.
   967	#   2. `CEREMONY_EFFECTIVE` is NOT flipped. Flipping it would ALSO re-enable
   968	#      the ROOT surfaces (root .gitignore blocks, PROTOCOL.md, SPEC/v1) for a
   969	#      directory whose ceremony is UNKNOWN — reinstating precisely the
   970	#      cross-boundary write that re-pass rc.4 t2 P2 removed, because a
   971	#      pre-v1.2 `--ceremony user` install carries the marker too. The
   972	#      amendment widens the DELIVERY decision, which is what the Owner
   973	#      ratified, and nothing else. Widening it further is a separate decision
   974	#      with its own evidence.
