  1281	# "link" tolerates a symlinked LEAF, anything else (default "file") does not.
  1282	# A `LINK  <relpath>  <target>` record describes a --mode link delivery whose
  1283	# leaf IS a symlink by construction, so rejecting it here silently dropped the
  1284	# record from the sanitized manifest: _baseline_has_spec_record and both
  1285	# readlink-vs-recorded-target checks could then NEVER match, and every
  1286	# link-mode upgrade lost framework ownership of SPEC/v1 and the marker, with
  1287	# marker-first readers falling back to the stale root VERSION (codex W1
  1288	# round 6, P2). The leaf is never FOLLOWED here — validation stays at the
  1289	# consumers, which compare `readlink` against the recorded target. Hash
