   373	  .claude/.framework-version for the installed framework version). NOTE: .claude/settings.json IS
   374	  updated in place by the default-on baseline migration (the model/permission
   375	  leaf keys: model, availableModels, fallbackModel, permissions.defaultMode)
   376	  and the idempotent settings-merge (new lifecycle-hook registrations) —
   377	  adopter-CUSTOMIZED values are always preserved with a named warning, and a
   378	  pre-migration backup is written to .claude.bak/. Opt out with
   379	  --no-settings-migrate / --no-settings-merge to manage settings.json by hand.
   380	
   381	Options:
   382	  --profile <list>      Comma-separated profiles to refresh (default: core,frontend).
   383	                        Available: core, frontend, <domain-name>.
   384	                        Example: --profile core,fintech
   385	  --stack <name>        Stack-specific hooks override (default: none).
   386	                        Example: --stack node
   387	  --pin <tag>           Pin source to specific tag/SHA (SPEC v1 install-cli.md).
   388	                        Refuses if target has uncommitted .claude/ changes.
   389	                        Example: --pin v1.18.0
   390	  --dry-run             Print what WOULD be replaced without modifying $TARGET.
   391	  --no-diff-warn        Silence the F-CHAOS-3 "customization will be replaced" warnings.
   392	  --no-deprecation-warn Silence the PLAN-135 advisory model-deprecation scan
   393	                        (the scan never blocks the upgrade either way).
   394	  --no-settings-merge   Skip the PLAN-135 W2 idempotent settings-merge step
   395	                        that registers new lifecycle hooks (the Setup
   396	                        post-install self-verification hook, and the PLAN-179
   397	                        W1-b SessionStart/compact constraint-pinning hook)
   398	                        into the adopter's existing .claude/settings.json.
   399	                        Skipping leaves those channels UNWIRED on an already
   400	                        installed repo. The merge is idempotent
   401	                        + fail-open (never blocks the upgrade); pass this to opt
   402	                        out entirely and manage settings.json by hand.
   403	  --no-settings-migrate PLAN-163 T5.4: skip the baseline-aware settings
   404	                        migration (model, availableModels, fallbackModel,
   405	                        permissions.defaultMode + T3.4-gated new-event
   406	                        registrations). 3-state policy per LEAF KEY:
   407	                        absent -> write the new baseline; equal to the OLD
   408	                        baseline (byte-compared) -> update; customized ->
   409	                        PRESERVE + named WARNING. Idempotent + fail-open;
   410	                        never blocks the upgrade.
   411	  --settings-migrate-only
   412	                        Run ONLY the T5.4 settings baseline migration
   413	                        against <target-repo-path> and exit 0 (test/ops
   414	                        seam; honors --dry-run + --no-settings-migrate).
   415	  --print-settings-baselines
   416	                        Print the normative T5.4 baseline table (JSON) and
   417	                        exit 0. Oracles derive their expectations from this
   418	                        output instead of hardcoding the literals.
   419	  --no-replay           PLAN-153 Wave B (B2): do NOT replay the recorded
   420	                        install request from .claude/.install-state.json.
   421	                        By default, when that file exists and validates,
   422	                        --profile/--stack DEFAULT to the recorded values
   423	                        (explicit flags always win), and request.github_owner
   424	                        is what renders .github/CODEOWNERS (rail round-7 F4).
   425	                        With --no-replay the handle is treated as unknown and
   426	                        the .github/CODEOWNERS.template branch applies, exactly
   427	                        as for an install that never passed --github-owner.
   428	                        Missing/invalid state falls back to the ADR-155
   429	                        drift-classifier path — never an error, never a no-op.
   430	  --harness <c|codex>   PLAN-155 Wave 5: override the harness. Defaults to the
   431	                        recorded request.harness (B2 replay). When codex, the
   432	                        upgrade also refreshes the .codex/ bundle from the
   433	                        current templates (collision behavior follows
   434	                        --on-conflict; refuse leaves local edits).
   435	  --managed-hooks       PLAN-155 Wave 5 (codex): also refresh requirements.toml
   436	                        (managed-hooks posture). Replayed from state otherwise.
   437	  --skip <glob>         Exclude files from the overwrite (repeat for multiple globs).
   438	                        Example: --skip='.claude/scripts/local/*'
   439	  --skip=<glob>         Alternate inline syntax for --skip.
   440	  --ceremony <maintainer|user>
   441	                        Re-pass rc.4 t3/t5: explicit ceremony for PRE-STATE
   442	                        targets (no readable .claude/.install-state.json).
   443	                        A RECORDED ceremony in the install state ALWAYS wins
   444	                        over this flag; with neither record nor flag the
   445	                        upgrade fails safe to 'user' (root files untouched)
   446	                        and that inference is never persisted. Only an
   447	                        explicit flag/env or a recorded value persists.
   448	                        Env override: CEO_UPGRADE_CEREMONY=<maintainer|user>.
   449	  --purge-misinstalled  PLAN-161 U3 (opt-in — NEVER default): delete files found
   450	                        inside the framework-internal excluded trees
   451	                        (.claude/hooks/{tests,legacy}, .claude/scripts/tests,
   452	                        .claude/hooks/_lib/tests + test_isolation.py/testing.py)
   453	                        ONLY when their sha256 matches the current framework
   454	                        source at the SAME relpath or the recorded baseline
   455	                        digest for that relpath. Every purged file is backed up
   456	                        to .claude.bak/ first; symlinks are never followed.
   457	                        Without this flag (and always under --dry-run) the scan
   458	                        only PREVIEWS would-purge candidates.
   459	  --on-conflict <mode>  PLAN-138 Wave C (ADR-155): how to handle a CONFLICT — a
   460	                        file that differs from BOTH the recorded install
   461	                        baseline AND the new framework source (adopter and
   462	                        framework both changed it). One of:
   463	                          refuse  (default) per-file skip + report, never abort
   464	                          theirs  overwrite with the framework version
   465	                          backup  overwrite, original preserved in .claude.bak/
   466	                        Requires a baseline manifest; without one the upgrade
   467	                        falls back to today's diff -q warn-then-clobber.
   468	  -h, --help            Show this help and exit 0.
   469	
   470	Backup behavior:
   471	  Files about to be overwritten are first copied to .claude.bak/{timestamp}/
   472	  inside $TARGET. If a customization exists at the destination, a `diff -q`
   473	  WARNING is emitted on stderr (suppressible via --no-diff-warn).
   474	
   475	Exit codes:
   476	  0 — upgrade completed (or --help / --dry-run preview)
   477	  1 — bad usage / unknown option / missing target
   478	  2 — target has uncommitted .claude/ changes when --pin was passed
   479	  3 — every other upgrade step completed, but the docs/ + .github/ delivery
   480	      FAILED its precondition (unreadable or poisoned delivery-route table).
   481	      See the 'PRECONDITION FAILED' line in the output for which one.
   482	
   483	Notes:
   484	  Run after `git pull` in the source ceo-orchestration repo. The upgrade
   485	  refreshes the PROTOCOL.md pointer to keep the adopter aligned with the
   486	  current source layout (DevOps-P1-4).
   487	
   488	See also:
   489	  scripts/install.sh --help     for fresh-install flags + profile semantics
   490	  INSTALL.md §Upgrade flow      for the full upgrade walk-through
   491	HELP
   492	      exit 0
   493	      ;;
   494	    -*)
   495	      echo "ERROR: unknown option: $1" >&2
   496	      exit 1
   497	      ;;
   498	    *)
   499	      TARGET="$1"
   500	      shift
   501	      ;;
   502	  esac
   503	done
   504	
   505	if [[ -z "$TARGET" || ! -d "$TARGET" ]]; then
   506	  echo "Usage: $0 <target-repo-path> [--profile <list>] [--stack <name>] [--pin <tag>] [--dry-run] [--ceremony <maintainer|user>]" >&2
   507	  exit 1
   508	fi
